  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "TRIAL EDITION - SQL longer than 10,000 characters is rejected (parse() returns -1). Full edition: https://www.sqlparser.com\n\nRelease 4.1.0.15\n\n- [DB2] Accept the CURRENT MEMBER special register, for example\n  SELECT ... FROM TABLE(SYSPROC.ENV_GET_SYSTEM_RESOURCES())\n  WHERE MEMBER = CURRENT MEMBER WITH UR. It previously failed with a\n  syntax error near MEMBER. CURRENT MEMBER is now accepted wherever\n  an expression is allowed and is parsed as a constant, like\n  CURRENT SCHEMA. MEMBER can still be used as a column name.\n\nDemos: https://github.com/sqlparser/gsp_demo_dotnet",
